    "body": "<h2 id=\"982b4af39473\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Use <strong>Comments</strong> in Klaviyo's drag-and-drop email editor to leave feedback directly on email blocks, reply to teammates, and track outstanding changes — all without leaving the editor. Faster review cycles mean fewer back-and-forth messages and quicker send times.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"ed0bf5b390dd\">Before you begin</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Comments are available in the drag-and-drop <strong>Email Editor</strong> only. They are not available in SMS, push notifications, or forms.</li>\n<li>You must have a <strong>Content Creator</strong>, <strong>Campaign Coordinator</strong>, <strong>Manager</strong>, <strong>Administrator</strong>, or <strong>Owner</strong> role to add, edit, delete, resolve, or react to comments. Users with the <strong>Analyst</strong> role can read and view comments but cannot write them.</li>\n<li>Users in <strong>read-only</strong> mode (no template editing access) will not see the block-level comment button.</li>\n<li>Comments are tied to the template — anyone with access to the template can see all threads.</li>\n<li>Estimated time: <strong>1–2 minutes</strong> to leave a comment; real-time updates mean teammates see it immediately.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"1cfee7bd2c7c\">Overview</h2>\n<p>Comments let your team collaborate directly on an email before it sends. You can:</p>\n<p></p>\n<ul>\n<li>add a comment to any specific block in the email,</li>\n<li>reply to existing comment threads,</li>\n<li>edit or delete your own comments,</li>\n<li>resolve or unresolve a thread once feedback is addressed,</li>\n<li>react to comments with emoji,</li>\n<li>mention teammates with @ to notify them directly, and</li>\n<li>control how you're notified about new activity.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<p>Comments are scoped to the template and update in real time — no refresh needed. The original email content is never changed by leaving a comment; comments are a layer on top of the design.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"7ec0d7323a31\">Set it up</h2>\n<h3 id=\"9f9f3740b11e\">Open the comments panel</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open any email from <strong>Templates</strong>, <strong>Campaigns &gt; Email</strong>, or <strong>Flows &gt; Email</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the top-right corner of the editor header, click the <strong>speech bubble</strong> icon. A badge on the icon shows the number of unresolved or unread threads.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Comments</strong> panel slides open on the right side of the canvas. All existing threads for this email are listed here.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<p><strong>Tip</strong>: Click the icon again at any time to collapse the panel without losing your place in the editor.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"73954b83972e\">Add a comment to a block</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Hover over any block on the canvas. A quick-action toolbar appears above the block.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>comment</strong> icon (speech bubble) in the toolbar.</li>\n<li>A comment composer appears. Type your feedback — you can use <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, <s>strikethrough</s>, and emoji.</li>\n<li>To notify a specific teammate, type @ followed by their name and select them from the dropdown.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Submit</strong> to post the comment. A small avatar indicator appears at the right edge of the block, showing that it has an active thread.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<p><strong>Tip</strong>: You can also start from the Comments panel — open it first, then click into the block you want to annotate.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"dd930ea49011\">Reply to a thread</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>In the <strong>Comments</strong> panel, click any existing thread to open the detail view.</li>\n<li>Type your reply in the composer at the bottom of the thread.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Submit</strong>. Replies appear in chronological order below the original comment.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"3581e8ec4dbc\">Resolve a thread</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the thread in the <strong>Comments</strong> panel.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Resolve</strong> in the thread header. The thread moves to the resolved view and the block indicator disappears from the canvas.</li>\n<li>To reopen a resolved thread, use the filter at the top of the panel to show <strong>Resolved</strong> threads, then click <strong>Unresolve</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<p><strong>Tip</strong>: Any team member with write access can resolve or unresolve any thread — you don't have to be the original author.</p>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"c96a8c13e1bb\">Edit or delete your own comments</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Hover over your comment in a thread. A <strong>···</strong> (more) menu appears.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Edit</strong> to update the comment body, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Delete</strong> to remove the comment. The comment body is replaced with a placeholder to preserve thread continuity.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"9368d395615e\">React to a comment</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Hover over any comment in a thread.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>emoji</strong> icon that appears.</li>\n<li>Select a reaction. Your avatar is shown on the reaction so teammates know who reacted.</li>\n<li>Click the same reaction again to remove it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>\n<h3 id=\"e609c1b4a5b0\">Manage notification settings</h3>\n<p>By default, you'll receive email notifications for all new activity on templates you've commented on.</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the <strong>Comments</strong> panel, click the <strong>gear</strong> (⚙) icon in the panel header.</li>\n<li>Choose one of three settings:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>All activity</strong> — notifies you of every new comment and reply on this template.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Mentions only</strong> — notifies you only when someone @mentions you.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Off</strong> — disables all notifications for this template.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Your preference is saved automatically.</li>\n</ol>",
